1. THE LAW: A ∪ ∅ = A, A ∩ U = A
   checked on all 16 choices of 1 subset(s) of U = {1, 2, 3, 4}: True

2. ONE INSTANCE, WORKED
   A = {1, 2}, B = {2, 3}, C = {3, 4}, A' = {3, 4}, B' = {1, 4}
   A ∪ ∅ = {1, 2} = A
   A ∩ U = {1, 2} = A

3. THE SAME LAW IN LOGIC: p ∨ false = p, p ∧ true = p
   every row of the truth table agrees, which is why the member-by-member check is a proof:
   p   left  right
   T   T     T
   F   T     T
